Module 10 — Toriloshop: Full CRUD
Project Description
This module implements complete Create, Read, Update, and Delete (CRUD) functionality for both products and categories in the Toriloshop Django project. Users can add new products and categories via validated forms, edit existing entries with pre-filled forms, and delete records through a confirmation page. Flash messages provide feedback after every action, and a search feature allows filtering products by name.

Features Implemented
Products
FeatureURLDescriptionList all products/products/Displays all products; supports search by nameView product detail/products/<pk>/Shows full details of a single productAdd product/products/add/Form to create a new product with validationEdit product/products/<pk>/edit/Pre-filled form to update an existing productDelete product/products/<pk>/delete/Confirmation page; deletes only on POST
Categories
FeatureURLDescriptionList all categories/categories/Displays all categories with product countAdd category/categories/add/Form to create a new categoryEdit category/categories/<pk>/edit/Pre-filled form to update a categoryDelete category/categories/<pk>/delete/Confirmation page; deletes only on POST
Additional Features

Flash messages — success messages shown after every create, edit, and delete action
CSRF protection — all forms include {% csrf_token %}
Form validation — price must be greater than 0, stock cannot be negative
Search — product list can be filtered by name via a search query parameter


Setup Instructions
1. Clone the repository
bashgit clone https://github.com/your-username/firstname-lastname-backend-dune-cohort.git
cd firstname-lastname-backend-dune-cohort/module-10
2. Create and activate a virtual environment
bashpython -m venv venv

# Windows
venv\Scripts\activate

# Mac/Linux
source venv/bin/activate
3. Install dependencies
bashpip install django
4. Run migrations
bashpython manage.py makemigrations
python manage.py migrate
5. Create a superuser (for admin access)
bashpython manage.py createsuperuser
6. Run the development server
bashpython manage.py runserver
Visit http://127.0.0.1:8000 in your browser.